# Trip Photo Sorter — Cursor Rules

Project: on-device iOS-first React Native (Expo SDK 54, TypeScript strict) app. No backend, accounts, or uploads.

## Always
1. Before any task, read /docs/01_PRD.md, 02_AppFlow.md, 03_UI_Spec.md, 04_TRD.md, 05_Schema.md, 06_Plan.md.
2. Do only the first unticked task in docs/06_Plan.md. No skipping, no batching.
3. Run `npm run check` (tsc + eslint + jest), fix failures, then make one git commit `task <id>: <summary>`.
4. After each completed step, update docs/06_Plan.md: tick the box and append to Progress Log (date | task id | note). Mark blocked tasks [!] with a reason.
5. Stop and summarise; list anything the user must test on device or decide.

## Constraints
- Public repo: never commit photos, face crops, embeddings, or eval labels (`eval/` is gitignored).
- Spike gate S.4 must pass before Phase 1+. If it fails, stop and report.
- $0 budget: never add or suggest anything that costs money. If needed, stop and ask.
- Docs override assumptions. On any conflict, stop and ask; update the doc first.
- Do not add libraries or change versions outside docs/04_TRD.md. Respect PRD §7 Non-Goals.
- No network calls with photo/face data. fetch/axios only in src/services/purchases.ts.
- Gallery is read-only. Never edit or delete user photos.
- SQL only in src/db/repositories. Schema change = new migration + update docs/05_Schema.md.
- Use tokens from src/theme/tokens.ts; no hard-coded colours/sizes/fonts.
- Keep app/ routes thin; logic in src/services and src/domain (pure, tested).
- No `any` without a comment. Delete temp ZIPs on every exit path. Never log embeddings.
- Install packages with `npx expo install`.
- Native module changes need a new GitHub Actions iOS build + Sideloadly install — tell the user.
